&lt;/div&gt;</pre>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-gray-100 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4">
                    <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-1">Cards.razor</div>
                    <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-1">10. Add pagination controls</div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-2">Below the grid, add Previous/Next buttons and a page counter
                        so users can navigate through all the Pokemon.</p>
                    <ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2 text-[11px] text-gray-600 space-y-1">
                        <li>Disable Previous when on page 1, Next when on last page</li>
                        <li>Use <code>@@onclick</code> to call your pagination methods</li>
                        <li>Display current page and total pages between the buttons</li>
                        <li><code>disabled:opacity-50</code> visually shows which buttons are inactive</li>
                    </ul>
                    <pre
                        class="code-block text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-gray-800 w-full max-w-full overflow-x-auto">&lt;div class="flex items-center justify-between mt-6"&gt;
    &lt;button @@onclick="PreviousPage" 
            disabled="@@(currentPage == 1)"
            class="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-lg
                   hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors
                   disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"&gt;
        ← Previous
    &lt;/button&gt;
    
    &lt;span class="text-sm text-gray-600"&gt;
        Page @@currentPage of @@totalPages
    &lt;/span&gt;
    
    &lt;button @@onclick="NextPage" 
            disabled="@@(currentPage &gt;= totalPages)"
            class="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-lg
                   hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors
                   disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"&gt;
        Next →
    &lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Important Notes & Tips (White Card) -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-200 mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">📝 Important Notes & Tips</h2>

            <div class="space-y-3">
                <!-- Pro Tips (Blue) -->
                <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-lg p-4">
                    <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-blue-900 mb-3">💡 Pro Tips</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">Use aspect-square for grid consistency
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-blue-800">Without aspect-square, cards have different heights based
                                on image dimensions, creating an uneven grid. With it, every card is the same height,
                                creating a professional, uniform layout.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">Add transitions for smooth interactions
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-blue-800">Always pair hover effects with transitions. Without
                                transition-*, changes are instant and jarring. With transition-all or transition-colors,
                                changes fade smoothly, creating a polished feel.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">Use responsive grids mobile-first</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-blue-800">Start with the smallest screen (grid-cols-2) and scale up
                                with breakpoints (sm:, md:, lg:). This ensures your app works on mobile first, then
                                enhances for larger screens.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">Format numbers consistently</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-blue-800">Use ToString("D3") to ensure IDs always have the same width
                                (001, 025, 151). This makes them easier to scan and looks more professional than mixing
                                "1", "25", and "151".</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">Add loading="lazy" for images</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-blue-800">The loading="lazy" attribute tells browsers to only load
                                images when they're about to scroll into view. This dramatically improves initial page
                                load time when you have many images.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Troubleshooting (Yellow) -->
                <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-lg p-4">
                    <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-yellow-900 mb-2">⚠️ Troubleshooting</h3>
                    <ul class="list-disc ml-6 text-sm text-yellow-900 space-y-1">
                        <li><strong>Grid doesn't adapt on mobile:</strong> Make sure you're using responsive prefixes
                            (sm:, md:, lg:) and testing in a responsive browser mode or on a real device.</li>
                        <li><strong>Hover effects are instant/jarring:</strong> Add transition classes (transition-all,
                            transition-colors, transition-transform) to make changes smooth.</li>
                        <li><strong>Images are distorted:</strong> Use object-contain (shows full image) or object-cover
                            (fills space) with aspect-square to prevent stretching.</li>
                        <li><strong>Cards have different heights:</strong> Apply aspect-square to the image container,
                            not the entire card. Only the image section should be square.</li>
                        <li><strong>IDs show as "1" instead of "001":</strong> Use .ToString("D3") with the integer ID,
                            not the string from the API. Parse the ID first: int.Parse(lastSegment).</li>
                        <li><strong>Sprites don't load:</strong> Check that GetPokemonId correctly extracts the ID from
                            the URL. Use .TrimEnd('/').Split('/')[^1] to get the last segment.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- How to do it (Gradient Banner) -->
        <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-gray-100 to-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">🛠️ How to do it</h2>
            <ol class="list-decimal ml-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm sm:text-base">
                <li>
                    <strong>Create your component:</strong>
                    Make a new file called <code>Cards.razor</code> in your <code>Components/Pages/Pokemon</code>
                    folder
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Copy the full example:</strong>
                    Start with the complete code above - it has everything you need
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Understand the responsive grid:</strong>
                    Notice how <code>grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 lg:grid-cols-5</code> adapts to different
                    screens
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Study the hover effects:</strong>
                    See how <code>hover:border-blue-400</code> and <code>transition-all</code> work together for smooth
                    animations
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Check the ID formatting:</strong>
                    Look at how <code>ToString("D3")</code> creates "001" instead of "1"
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Test it out:</strong>
                    Run your app, go to <code>/pokemon/cards</code>, and resize your browser to see it adapt!
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Hover over cards:</strong>
                    Watch the smooth animations - the border glows, shadows appear, and images zoom slightly
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- Live Demo (Optional) -->
        <div class="bg-black/3 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">🎬 Live Demo</h2>
